      "message": "Cool.  Note that I landed a CL that makes arm64 100% complete neon.\nI plan to do a pass to fill in the 32 bit arm, which is important for embedded, and may do mve which is a relatively direct port\n\nThis datatype - ARGB4444 and the other 2 16 bit RGB formats, are not 100% optimized on other platforms, and I think should be considered deprecated, because they were requested/used as early display and gpu formats, but they are replaced with better display/gpu formats in the future.  10 bit formats are emerging as more important and so far AR30/AB30 for argb, and P010 for yuv.",
